    "blocks": [
      {
        "id": "textbook-exception-definition",
        "moduleId": "intro-definition",
        "depth": "core",
        "kind": "definition",
        "title": "教材定义：exception 是什么",
        "markdown": "教材把 **exception** 定义为一个对象：当错误发生时，它可以被方法抛出（thrown 或 raised），并由调用代码捕获（caught 或 handled）。\n\n这里有两个关键点：exception 本身是一个对象，而不是一个布尔标志或错误码；它的作用发生在“抛出”和“捕获”两端，抛出方报告错误，捕获方决定如何处理。",
        "provenance": {
          "origin": "textbook",
          "representation": "paraphrase",
          "sourceSpans": [
            {
              "materialId": "doc-d998d2c477335adeea4bf2f2",
              "blockIds": [
                "block-000078"
              ],
              "headingPath": [
                "Lifecycle of an Object",
                "Exceptions"
              ],
              "lineStart": 494,
              "lineEnd": 498,
              "assetRefs": [],
              "excerptSha256": "b85730a716fb1648181431963908bed5b6dc56551a5b79af2b69f8fbd6e4fc21"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "model-package-intuition",
        "moduleId": "intro-definition",
        "depth": "support",
        "kind": "explanation",
        "title": "模型补充：把 exception 想成贴了标签的包裹",
        "markdown": "可以把 exception 想成一个代表错误的包裹：出错的方法把包裹交给上一层调用者，直到有人愿意接手处理。\n\n这个类比强调了教材定义中的两点：包裹本身是一个对象；“交给上一层”则意味着由调用方、而不是抛出方法，来决定后续怎么处理。",
        "provenance": {
          "origin": "model",
          "basedOnBlockIds": [
            "textbook-exception-definition"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "textbook-throw-catch",
        "moduleId": "throw-catch-roles",
        "depth": "core",
        "kind": "mechanism",
        "title": "教材机制：抛出与捕获的分工",
        "markdown": "教材把 exception 的使用拆成两段职责：\n\n- **抛出**：方法在错误发生时把 exception 对象抛出（throw 或 raise）。\n- **捕获**：调用代码捕获它并决定如何处理（catch 或 handle）。\n\n因此 exception 不是被抛出的方法自行“解决”的错误；它把错误上报给调用方，由调用方选择响应方式。",
        "provenance": {
          "origin": "textbook",
          "representation": "paraphrase",
          "sourceSpans": [
            {
              "materialId": "doc-d998d2c477335adeea4bf2f2",
              "blockIds": [
                "block-000078"
              ],
              "headingPath": [
                "Lifecycle of an Object",
                "Exceptions"
              ],
              "lineStart": 494,
              "lineEnd": 498,
              "assetRefs": [],
              "excerptSha256": "b85730a716fb1648181431963908bed5b6dc56551a5b79af2b69f8fbd6e4fc21"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "model-flow-separation",
        "moduleId": "throw-catch-roles",
        "depth": "core",
        "kind": "explanation",
        "title": "模型补充：错误处理如何与正常流程分离",
        "markdown": "把职责分给抛出方与捕获方，会带来一个重要结构：**正常代码只描述成功路径，错误处理集中在捕获处**。\n\n抛出方法不必在每个调用点都插入状态判断，调用方也不必逐步检查返回值；它只需在愿意处理错误的位置包住相关调用。异常从抛出点向上寻找处理者，找不到处理者时才会成为未捕获异常。",
        "provenance": {
          "origin": "model",
          "basedOnBlockIds": [
            "textbook-throw-catch"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "textbook-terminology-note",
        "moduleId": "throw-catch-roles",
        "depth": "support",
        "kind": "note",
        "title": "教材说明：throw/catch 与 raise/handle",
        "markdown": "教材指出，面向对象语言更倾向使用 **throw/catch** 的说法，而不是 **raise/handle**。\n\n两套词描述的是同一件事：throw 对应 raise（抛出），catch 对应 handle（捕获并处理）。阅读不同语言或不同教材时，不应把它们当成两种不同的机制。",
        "provenance": {
          "origin": "textbook",
          "representation": "paraphrase",
          "sourceSpans": [
            {
              "materialId": "doc-d998d2c477335adeea4bf2f2",
              "blockIds": [
                "block-000078"
              ],
              "headingPath": [
